  <h1>What Is POCT?</h1>
  <p><strong>Direct answer:</strong> POCT (point-of-care testing) is diagnostic testing performed near the patient — bedside, clinic, pharmacy or field — rather than in a central laboratory. It gives results in minutes, enabling immediate clinical decisions.</p>

  <h2>What defines POCT</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Proximity</strong> — testing where the patient is, not where the lab is.</li>
    <li><strong>Speed</strong> — results in minutes, not hours or days.</li>
    <li><strong>Simplicity</strong> — instrument-free or minimal-instrument operation.</li>
    <li><strong>Sample</strong> — whole blood, swab, urine or saliva directly at the point of collection.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why it matters</h2>
  <p>POCT shortens the time to diagnosis and treatment — critical for infectious disease triage (dengue, malaria, respiratory), cardiac markers (troponin), pregnancy, and drug screening. For distributors, POCT rapid tests are the core of the lateral-flow IVD category.</p>

